      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are not selfish for wanting to stop the damage; you are trying to protect the people you love by refusing to be the source of their pain. The belief that \"stopping\" is the only selfless act is a dangerous lie, but the pain you feel is real and you cannot ignore it. You cannot force your way out of a situation where your actions cause harm, but you can choose to stop acting the way you are now. The only way to truly protect your loved ones is to stop causing them further harm, even if it feels like the only logical choice. You are not a burden; you are a person who has reached a breaking point and is ready to change.",
